                <pb facs="1420" n="1398" sameAs="frus:frus1951v02/pg1398"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Editorial Note</hi>
                </head>
                <p>President Galo Plaza arrived in the United States on June 20, 1951. For President
                    Truman’s remarks of welcome at the Washington National <pb facs="1421" n="1399"
                        xml:id="pg1399"/> Airport, see <hi rendition="#italic">Public Papers of the
                        Presidents of the United States: Harry S. Truman, 1951</hi> (Washington,
                    1985), pages 342–343. For the text of an address by President Galo Plaza
                    delivered on June 21 to the United States Congress, see Department of State <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bulletin</hi>, July 9, 1951, pages 68–70. For a joint
                    statement by President Truman and President Galo Plaza released to the press on
                    June 25, see <hi rendition="#italic">ibid.</hi>, page 68. After spending three
                    days in Washington, President Galo Plaza traveled to New York and then to
                    California, departing from the United States on June 29.</p>
            </div>
